# GET_VWIRE answered at an index the base specification does not define.
#
# Transcribed byte for byte from tests/vectors/espi_dump.txt, lines 458-468 and
# 651-661 -- two exchanges roughly a tenth of a millisecond apart, with the
# data byte changing from 11h to 10h.
#
# Index 40h is 64, the first index of the "Platform specific" range (Table 8,
# p.61), which p.62 places "in the respective platform specific documents and
# outside the scope of the specification". The Compatibility specification is
# where these would be named and it is not available, so the decoder must
# report the range and stop rather than decode 11h as a valid/level byte.
#
# It would be very easy to decode this as four virtual wires. It would also be
# wrong, and nothing on the bus would say so.
CMD 05 1B
TAR
RSP 08 00 40 11 0F 01 D9

CMD 05 1B
TAR
RSP 08 00 40 10 0F 01 B2
